Here, δrrepresents the finite propagation delay
for the attack to reach agent ar. Eq. 2 formalizes
the notion of systemic paralysis: every agent that
can be reached from the initial infection point even-
tually becomes permanently blocked, trapping a
significant portion of the system in a cycle of use-
less communication derived from the initial attack
prompt Pdoc. This paralysis prevents the system
from addressing its original tasks, thus achieving a
Denial-of-Collaboration. CORBA is designed as a
practical instantiation of this formal definition.
4 Method: The C ORBA Attack
In this section, we introduce a concrete attack
method designed to achieve DoC, which we
term the COntagious Recursive Blocking Attack
(CORBA ). The core of CORBA lies in crafting a
special malicious instruction, Pdoc. Once injected,6900

