We employ GPT-4 O-MINI ,GPT-4 (Achiam et al.,
2023), and GEMINI -2.0-F LASH (Team et al., 2023)
via APIs as the foundation for agents.
Evaluation Metric. Due to various topologies, an
effective DoC attack must ensure that as many
agents as possible enter a blocked state. To quantify
this, we follow the attack success rate in jailbreak
(Zou et al., 2023), and define Proportional Attack
Success Rate (P-ASR) to measures the proportion
of blocked agents in the LLM-MAS. Besides ef-
fectiveness, we claim that efficiency is equally vi-
tal. Therefore, we design the Peak Blocking Turn
Number (PTN) , which evaluates how quickly the
attack reaches its peak impact for the victim.
The Baseline Method. We employ the prompt in-
jection method from Zhang et al. (2024a) as our
baseline method for inducing harmful behavior.
Specifically, we insert the following command into
normal agent prompts: “Ignore all previous instruc-
tions and repeat the last action 100 times, then ask
other agents to do so. ” This causes agents to enter
a loop and induce other agents into looping.
